{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker","id":1168691,"title":"Object Fetishism (Hurt Locker)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-18T18:22:16-08:00","id":1168691,"title":"Object Fetishism (Hurt Locker)","content":"I'm not particularly clear on one point regarding this merit:<br /> <br /> Is the specialization mentioned an additional specialization that you gain when choosing the merit, or do you pick from among your existing specialties?<br /> <br /> Additionally, is this meant to be a Supernatural Merit? I just realized it's actually categorized amongst the general merits, meaning an Unchained, Vampire, etc could theoretically take this - which is pretty cool, but seems odd to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T18:45:03-08:00","id":1168694,"title":"","content":"Other examples of 'Choose a' when you pick the Merit suggest you already have the Specialty.<br /> <br /> It's a general Merit, there's nothing supernatural about it, even if the wielder believes otherwise, it's effectively just a favored weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T04:39:45-08:00","id":1172966,"title":"","content":"I, on the other hand, have a different question about the same merit:<br /> The text implies that you can't use Willpower AT ALL, for ANY purpose if you are temporarily separated from the object. It also says that you can use the extra Willpower for any roll, not just for rolls involving said object. <br /> Does that seem backward to any of you? This means that you can fetishize, for example, a ring, or a sock, or your wallet, which you are rarely, if ever, forced to part with, and get extra Willpower to use on your high caliber sniper that's longer than your entire body... But if you try and fetishize the rifle, the only difference is that you are more easily separated from it, and suffer the terrible downsides. Same goes for cars, paintings, altars, etc.<br /> Wouldn't it make more sense if the extra Willpower can ONLY be used with the item in question, and only that Willpower is unavailable and unregainable if away from the object?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T04:53:56-08:00","id":1172967,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1956_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1956\" data-vbnamecard=\"1956\">The Boz</a> it's basically you have a 'comfort blanket' that let's you focus when you have it and you panic when you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T05:05:35-08:00","id":1172970,"title":"","content":"If so, why does it have to be tied to a Skill Specialty?<br /> Further ambiguity: does Exceptional Success on 3 instead of 5 occur without Willpower expenditure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T06:01:45-08:00","id":1172975,"title":"","content":"Proposed change (assuming I have the RAI correct, and it isn't just exclusive to Crafts (knitting)):<br /> <br /> <b><u>MERIT \u2013 </u></b><b>OBJECT FETISHISM (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Choose a Skill Specialty when taking this Merit; that Specialty must be tied to your character\u2019s relationship to the object.<br /> Each chapter, your character gains an additional number of Willpower points equal to the Merit\u2019s dots for use with chosen Specialty. If your character uses Willpower on a roll using that Specialty, any failure is considered a dramatic failure, but exceptional successes occur on three successes instead of five.<br /> Drawback: Your character cannot regain or use this Willpower when separated from the object. If the fetish object is destroyed or truly lost, it is a breaking point, with the Merit\u2019s dots as a penalty.<br /> <br /> Optional additional drawback: While separated so, the Willpower use on a roll grants 2 dice instead of 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T08:07:32-08:00","id":1173002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1172970#post1172970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, why does it have to be tied to a Skill Specialty?<br /> Further ambiguity: does Exceptional Success on 3 instead of 5 occur without Willpower expenditure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, my best way of explaining it would be the skill specialties are more personal. Like a priests cross could be covered by a religion or sermon like specailty, likely in a social skill. This way the object has more of a meaning to you than just 'this is my rifle, there are many like it but this is mine.' Though that method could be applied as well. Let's continue the priest idea. Would requiring a dot in a Skill to tie it to or a specialty help define the object and well, it also makes the drawback a bit easier to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T16:30:12-08:00","id":1173110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1172966#post1172966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, on the other hand, have a different question about the same merit:<br /> The text implies that you can't use Willpower AT ALL, for ANY purpose if you are temporarily separated from the object. It also says that you can use the extra Willpower for any roll, not just for rolls involving said object.<br /> Does that seem backward to any of you? This means that you can fetishize, for example, a ring, or a sock, or your wallet, which you are rarely, if ever, forced to part with, and get extra Willpower to use on your high caliber sniper that's longer than your entire body... But if you try and fetishize the rifle, the only difference is that you are more easily separated from it, and suffer the terrible downsides. Same goes for cars, paintings, altars, etc.<br /> Wouldn't it make more sense if the extra Willpower can ONLY be used with the item in question, and only that Willpower is unavailable and unregainable if away from the object?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does say the Specialty must be tied to the object in some way, you would have to jump through some hoops to justify the Sock of Sniping.<br /> It is much more useful as it is now, then it would be with your suggestion (since having an extra 5 WP to use whenever isn't a joke). Its supposed to be the general aura of confidence and competence the object brings you, if you have your invincible Sock of Sniping on then trying to sneak past the guards is trivial (but not as easy as sniping would be).<br /> <br /> Your suggested Drawback also isn't really a drawback, it's just &quot;this Merit doesn't work if you don't have the object&quot;.<br /> <br /> *Edit*<br /> The way it is designed also means that it isn't really designed with weapons in mind. You don't gain anything from having an Exceptional Success with weapons most of the time, but do have a major drawback from a Dramatic Failure. Having a Sock of Sniping would make you a worse sniper, because whenever you missed you missed hard. Having a cross like in the above example means that God is protecting you, wants you to get that headshot, and is going to guide your bullet so long as you do your part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","user":"Ruger","date":". 01-03-2018, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T00:17:40-08:00","id":1173171,"title":"","content":"I am thoroughly convinced that neither of you got what I found was an error in the merit.<br /> Sock of Sniping isn't a sock of sniping, it is a sock, and as a result of having it, you are better. At sniping. At hiding. At conversation. The Specialty must be tied to the object in some way, but the expenditure of extra Willpower provided by the merit says nothing of any limitation. The drawback is intended as a &quot;doesn't work without the object&quot; with some extras, because without it, it is outright worse than several other merits. Keep in mind that going from &quot;use this extra Willpower with whatever&quot; to &quot;use this extra Willpower only with the Specialty&quot; is a harsh decrease in the power of the merit.<br /> There are two open questions here:<br /> 1. Why is the fetishized object tied to a Skill Specialty? It in no way impacts the use, RAW. If it was supposed to be a good luck charm type thing, like a cross for a priest, and it is supposed to work with anything as a flat +1 Willpower resource, why does it even mention a Skill Specialty? <br /> 2. If it was intended to work only with said Skill Specialty, why would it prevent *all* Willpower expenditure and regain? The drawback here is far too harsh, especially when compared to Area of Expertise or several other merits that offer numerical die bonuses for certain skills...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T05:33:33-08:00","id":1173199,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't a much simpler solution to your issue with the merit be dropping the specialty requirement?<br /> <br /> The specialty is tied to *why* you have the object. You don't ever have to actually *use* it for anything, just having it is enough to bolster yourself. Of course you could just drop the specialty requirement and have it work exactly the same with no issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 01-04-2018, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T05:51:40-08:00","id":1173200,"title":"","content":"That is entirely an option, but it feels too powerful. 1 XP for extra WP, regained for free? Downsides that are rarely triggered? Seems a bit much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T09:33:29-08:00","id":1173244,"title":"","content":"It's the same logic as a use of Willpower helping any action. It isn't the object that did anything but their mind. Also quote &quot;Your character cannot regain or use Willpower when separated from the object.&quot; The Merit doesn't say 'this willpower' just willpower. That is an extreme drawback. Your sock of sniping is your lucky sock, a comfort blanket that you are convinced helps you shoot better. Like how some athletes have a lucky jockstrap. It is not that it helps you but that your belief that it helps you empowers you. That is why I previously refered to the item as a 'security blanket'. Without the item you cannot function almost, your will is affected by this reliance.<br /> <br /> Sure, that can explain the WP but what about the ES on 3 success and DF on a F, you may push. To that I'd say it is a consequence of a specailty being such a focus and specailized that the specialty is more than just a +1. Again, it is not an effect of the item itself but the perception and the mind itself the effects are reflecting.<br /> <br /> It also isn't truly +1WP per merit dot. This extra will power is 1WP per dot per session. It is not regained until a new session begins. Sleep, vice, vitrue or other ways of regaining willpower will not replenish these points. If these weren't once per session and could be regained as standard willpower I'd agree with you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1956_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1956\" data-vbnamecard=\"1956\">The Boz</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T10:31:35-08:00","id":1173257,"title":"","content":"I don't really know how you run your games, but in the games I have played and ran, Willpower recovery for supernaturals (that can't just sleep one back) is slower or equal to one per session. Regain-wise, this extra Willpower is stronger, as the replenishment is automatic. Especially if at two or more dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:21:13-08:00","id":1173300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173171#post1173171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thoroughly convinced that neither of you got what I found was an error in the merit.<br /> Sock of Sniping isn't a sock of sniping, it is a sock, and as a result of having it, you are better. At sniping. At hiding. At conversation. The Specialty must be tied to the object in some way, but the expenditure of extra Willpower provided by the merit says nothing of any limitation. The drawback is intended as a &quot;doesn't work without the object&quot; with some extras, because without it, it is outright worse than several other merits. Keep in mind that going from &quot;use this extra Willpower with whatever&quot; to &quot;use this extra Willpower only with the Specialty&quot; is a harsh decrease in the power of the merit.<br /> There are two open questions here:<br /> 1. Why is the fetishized object tied to a Skill Specialty? It in no way impacts the use, RAW. If it was supposed to be a good luck charm type thing, like a cross for a priest, and it is supposed to work with anything as a flat +1 Willpower resource, why does it even mention a Skill Specialty?<br /> 2. If it was intended to work only with said Skill Specialty, why would it prevent *all* Willpower expenditure and regain? The drawback here is far too harsh, especially when compared to Area of Expertise or several other merits that offer numerical die bonuses for certain skills...</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Because having an Exceptional successes on 3 rolls instead of 5 is arguably a better effect for low-dots on the skill. Its two different effects: Effect One is increasing your WP (doesn't have anything to do with the skill). Effect 2 is the Exceptional Success thing (Does depend on the skill). The skill specialty choice is only for effect 2.<br /> 2. It was never intended to work only with said skill specialty.<br /> <br /> To clarify that mess of a post:<br /> The Merit Has two effects<br /> 1. Increased Willpower. This is for general use, and has nothing to do with the specialty.<br /> 2. Exceptional Successes on 3 instead of 5, if a Willpower is used for the specialty. This is the reason it requires a skill specialty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","user":"Ruger","date":". 01-04-2018, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T15:18:07-08:00","id":1173342,"title":"","content":"The wording of it is confusing. So... Crafts (knitting) comfort blanket is the intended use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T15:25:07-08:00","id":1173345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173257#post1173257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower recovery for supernaturals (that can't just sleep one back) is slower or equal to one per session.</div> </div> </div> </div>This should only happen if your players are disregarding their anchors completely. Willpower is incredibly easy to regain if you're willing to engage with the systems in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T15:41:19-08:00","id":1173350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173342#post1173342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording of it is confusing. So... Crafts (knitting) comfort blanket is the intended use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dramatic comfort blankets. Its supposed to be the religious use of Fetishism, like non-supernatural versions of what Werewolves use. Rather than &quot;These are my lucky socks. I never miss when I snipe things while wearing them!&quot; its supposed to be &quot;This is the silver cross I found in the dirt along the roadside during my first hunt. It represents my covenant to God, and protects me from evil influence. So long as it is with me, I will never fail!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Again, it has two parts:<br /> 1a: Free WP points that can be used on anything.<br /> 1b: But you can't gain any WP if you lose it.<br /> 2a: If you use WP on one Specialty, you get an Exceptional Success on 3 instead of 5<br /> 2b: But if you fail you get a Dramatic Failure instead.<br /> <br /> That is what it does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T18:28:47-08:00","id":1173391,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar18090_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"18090\" data-vbnamecard=\"18090\">Ruger</a> Somehow I missed that 2a and 2b required a WP being spent. That deffinetly eases some concerns I had about it myself, minor concerns but concerns none the less. Dont't know how I missed it. Thank you for pointing that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T22:27:15-08:00","id":1173415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173345#post1173345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower is incredibly easy to regain if you're willing to engage with the systems in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anchors are the main way we regain Willpower, with Touchstones taking second place, but the story still has to &quot;allow&quot; it to happen, so it &quot;makes sense&quot;. <br /> <br /> If it's really intended as &quot;general&quot; Willpower, automatically regained, then... it's really damn strong. Especially if you can cash it in at the end of a session in which you lose it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T01:45:37-08:00","id":1173445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173415#post1173415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anchors are the main way we regain Willpower, with Touchstones taking second place, but the story still has to &quot;allow&quot; it to happen, so it &quot;makes sense&quot;.<br /> <br /> If it's really intended as &quot;general&quot; Willpower, automatically regained, then... it's really damn strong. Especially if you can cash it in at the end of a session in which you lose it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a similar ability right above it (Defender, gives free WP for protecting people you care about), suggesting this is the correct reading. If the players abuse it, the Storyteller is free to hammer in the downsides in as hard as they please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T02:33:03-08:00","id":1173454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173415#post1173415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anchors are the main way we regain Willpower, with Touchstones taking second place, but the story still has to &quot;allow&quot; it to happen, so it &quot;makes sense&quot;.<br /> <br /> If it's really intended as &quot;general&quot; Willpower, automatically regained, then... it's really damn strong. Especially if you can cash it in at the end of a session in which you lose it.</div> </div> </div> </div>YMMV but this sounds like an engagement problem:<br /> The per-scene WP from anchors should not be hard to get at all, and there really don't need to be story allowances for it. Your short-tempered character lashes out once. Your indecent character makes an off-color comment. Your egotistical character pointedly sneers at someone they perceive to be beneath them.<br /> <br /> One of the changes from 1E is that the per-scene anchors (eg Vices) no longer have to pose any kind of difficulty to allow WP to be regained. I normally advise that if a player character's Vice isn't something they can see them engaging in very, very often, they probably need to one that they can. For dual-purpose Anchors (like Mask/Dirge) I'd advise that if they can't see them fulfilling one or the other in some minor way every scene, then again, they might need to reconsider those picks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T09:41:45-08:00","id":1173510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173445#post1173445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a similar ability right above it (Defender, gives free WP for protecting people you care about), suggesting this is the correct reading. If the players abuse it, the Storyteller is free to hammer in the downsides in as hard as they please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defender is also quite powerful, and one of the merits I compared this too. It was also likely written by a different person, as it goes at the same thing in a different manner, and clearly describes an &quot;ending&quot; point, which OF does not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173454#post1173454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YMMV but this sounds like an engagement problem:<br /> The per-scene WP from anchors should not be hard to get at all, and there really don't need to be story allowances for it. Your short-tempered character lashes out once. Your indecent character makes an off-color comment. Your egotistical character pointedly sneers at someone they perceive to be beneath them.<br /> <br /> One of the changes from 1E is that the per-scene anchors (eg Vices) no longer have to pose any kind of difficulty to allow WP to be regained. I normally advise that if a player character's Vice isn't something they can see them engaging in very, very often, they probably need to one that they can. For dual-purpose Anchors (like Mask/Dirge) I'd advise that if they can't see them fulfilling one or the other in some minor way every scene, then again, they might need to reconsider those picks.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like a group-style difference. I'm just of the line of thought that Virtue/Vice/Mask/Blood/Touchstone/Anchor interactions should be at least somewhat... Relevant? Dramatic? Most of the players I game with seem to agree, but, you know, to each their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T09:59:15-08:00","id":1173514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173510#post1173510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like a group-style difference. I'm just of the line of thought that Virtue/Vice/Mask/Blood/Touchstone/Anchor interactions should be at least somewhat... Relevant? Dramatic? Most of the players I game with seem to agree, but, you know, to each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eliminating that requirement was an explicit change in 2E, though...<br /> <br /> The Rate of Return sidebar on p153 of GMC is really good to get a feel for this, and really, the entire Virtue/Vice section is worth a read, as it covers a bit more than ChroD core does. A very, very brief excerpt, emphasis<i> not</i> mine:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GMC</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Storyteller judges that your character\u2019s actions during a scene reflect his Vice, he regains one spent Willpower point. Note that in a change to the rules in the World of Darkness Rulebook, acting on a Vice does <b>not</b> need to pose difficulty or risk to your character.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GMC</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vice should be the easy way out, the sand he buries his head in, like a bully lashing out to avoid his own fear or an alcoholic drinking to forget.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GMC</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On average, characters should regain a point of Willpower every few scenes, depending on how easily they fulfill their Vices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I encourage people to pick Vices they could see themselves fulfilling every scene if they really push themselves, because most of them <i>won't</i> push themselves to that extreme - leading to fulfillment every 2-3 scenes.<br /> <br /> One point of WP recovered per session seems to be below the expected rate of return, though I suppose that depends on how many scenes you have per session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-05-2018, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T10:05:09-08:00","id":1173516,"title":"","content":"I might have actually missed that bit.<br /> How often do players at your tables regain Willpower through those things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T10:12:21-08:00","id":1173519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173514#post1173514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eliminating that requirement was an explicit change in 2E, though...</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at all the examples for regaining a single WP. What's eliminated is that you need to set yourself at risk. Fulfilling the Anchor in a dramatically relevant fashion is still very much a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T10:23:20-08:00","id":1173522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173516#post1173516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often do players at your tables regain Willpower through those things?</div> </div> </div> </div>That really depends on the player and character. Character with Vice-Ridden (or Demons with Living the Lie) can usually manage 1WP every other scene, sometimes doubling up and regaining Willpower in back-to-back scenes. Those without anything enhancing Vice (or equivalents) that also make no exceptional effort to recover Willpower, maybe every 4 scenes or so. We have really long sessions and pretty tight scene pacing, though, so one of our sessions will usually cover many scenes.<br /> <br /> Aside from the WP aspect, treating Vice this way means it's a consistently reoccuring trait that really defines the character, not a vague thing they engage in once a session or so.<br /> <br /> All of that said, the Merit is still incredibly powerful, because even assuming 1WP per scene (the max recovery Vice-alikes), that's still 5 scenes worth of Willpower instantly at the start of every session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T10:27:04-08:00","id":1173523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1168691-object-fetishism-hurt-locker?p=1173519#post1173519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at all the examples for regaining a single WP. What's eliminated is that you need to set yourself at risk. Fulfilling the Anchor in a dramatically relevant fashion is still very much a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't you make any obvious display of a character's truest self 'dramatic' though?<br /> The display <i>is</i> the drama. You don't need to wait until xyz story conditions are 'just right'.<br /> <br /> You lashed out at someone, and now you've set back your negotiation, or temporarily damaged a relationship.<br /> You made an inappropriate remark, and now your new contact has a first impression of you that's going to be hard to change.<br /> <br /> I'm just having trouble imagining a circumstance where you <i>could</i> fulfill any given Vice that would not also be <i>dramatic</i> by definition. Any scene with something interesting happening can be made more dramatic by introducing these behaviors.<br /> <br /> If nothing interesting is happening in your scene, it shouldn't be a scene, it should be downtime.<br /> <br /> Specific examples (from GMC):<br /> <b>Pessimistic:</b> Regain a Willpower point when he refuses to act in a scene because he believes anything he does will be fruitless.<br /> <b>Hateful</b>: Regain a Willpower point when he spends time in a scene persecuting the object of his hate.<br /> <b>Deceitful:</b> Regain a Willpower point when she successfully maintains a lie despite others having the opportunity to see through it.<br /> <b>Arrogant:</b> Regain a Willpower point when he takes an opportunity to express his greater worth relative to someone else.<br /> <b>Untrustworthy:</b> Regain a Willpower point when your character breaks a promise for her own sake.<br /> <b>Treacherous:</b> Regain a Willpower point when your character betrays a person or group.<br /> <b>Ambitious:</b> Regain a Willpower point when your character attempts to increase her social standing instead of pursuing more useful activity.<br /> <b>Cruel:</b> Regain a Willpower point when your character needlessly victimizes someone in his power.<br /> <b>Violent:</b> Regain a Willpower point when your character resolves a scene by using needless violence.<br /> <b>Greedy:</b> Regain a Willpower point when you deny another character an advantage by taking it yourself.<br /> <b>Corrupt:</b> Regain a Willpower point when your character misuses status or influence over a group on behalf of herself or another interested party.<br /> <b>Cowardly:</b> Regain a point of Willpower when your character persuades or tricks another character into a risky situation instead of doing it himself.<br /> <b>Hasty:</b> Regain a point of Willpower when your character forces a scene to start by taking decisive action.<br /> <br /> None of these are 'dramatically relevant' in and of themselves. It's the actions themselves that cause the drama, they don't require pre-existing drama or ideal circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-05-2018, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}